From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lena <lena@x>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:59:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] lena-0154: show ppid, P_* flags and thread count in the dump

The boot stalls right after "exec launchd_cache_loader" and every
observation costs a manual fastboot trip, so the process dump should answer
all of the obvious questions in one pass:

  SWEET PS: <pid> <ppid> <state> <p_flag> <threads> <comm> @<wchan> ...

  * absent            -> the exec never created the process
  * P_WEXIT/P_EXEC    -> stuck inside exec/exit
  * >1 thread         -> something in the process is still doing work
  * @<wchan>          -> the kernel wait channel (resolvable offline)
---
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -569,14 +569,22 @@
 
 	for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
 		struct uthread *ut;
+		int nthreads = 0;
 
 		if ((p = proc_find(pids[i])) == NULL) {
 			continue;
 		}
 		proc_lock(p);
-		printf("SWEET PS: %5d %c %.16s", (int)p->p_pid,
+		/* 0154: also show the parent, the P_* flags and the thread count -
+		 * one boot should be enough to tell "never started" (absent),
+		 * "stuck in exec" (P_WEXIT/P_EXEC) and "blocked" (wchan) apart. */
+		TAILQ_FOREACH(ut, &p->p_uthlist, uu_list) {
+			nthreads++;
+		}
+		printf("SWEET PS: %5d %5d %c %#06x %2d %.16s", (int)p->p_pid,
+		    (int)p->p_ppid,
 		    (p->p_stat > 0 && p->p_stat <= 5) ? " ?IRSZ"[p->p_stat] : '?',
-		    p->p_comm);
+		    p->p_flag, nthreads, p->p_comm);
 		TAILQ_FOREACH(ut, &p->p_uthlist, uu_list) {
 			if (ut->uu_wchan != NULL) {
 				printf(" @%p", ut->uu_wchan);
